  "worked_solution": "To find the coordinates of the point, we inspect its position along the $x$- and $y$-axes.\n\n* The point is $3$ units to the *right* of the origin, in the *positive* direction of the $x$-axis. So, its $x$-coordinate is $3.$\n\n* The point is $2$ units *below* the origin, in the *negative* direction of the $y$-axis. So, its $y$-coordinate is $-2.$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of our point are $(3,-2).$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
